      "writtenOn": "2023-09-05T21:03:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I updated this CL to just skip this step when running locally (i.e. when the `--local` flag is set). I\u0027m not sure if it makes sense to run `bazel clean` when running locally anyway.\n\nNote that the `/mnt/pd0` path is hardcoded in various task drivers already (try `$ git grep /mnt/pd0`). Example: https://skia.googlesource.com/skia/+/2b9fc6a2c250b16ce4b3a12e04dbf8b41ce8022f/infra/bots/task_drivers/bazel_build/bazel_build.go#67. Because of these hardcoded paths, I suspect that most such task drivers are actually impossible to run locally today.\n\nLet me know if you would like me to extract the hardcoded `/mnt/pd0` paths into command-line flags for all existing task drivers.",
      "parentUuid": "45c239f4_de38eb8a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "0a00a590272e5186556a71edd725cba7fc0446f3",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
